[{:db/id "q-18322/selection/983df087e2774509d32bf4ada481607a259c849b95031608b49f845cd218a233" :answer/id #uuid "3e49d3ec-f0aa-5abd-9ded-ed8c9885adeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{85}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18322/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" :answer/id #uuid "bc13e402-5e5b-5248-82fd-f71f12f35d1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18322/selection/5925bef74d9593b1a517c264a2c49ec5b06eb1da01b8b814c5455bf64faa0c2d" :answer/id #uuid "696a450b-0b6f-5d21-b2df-f450197f9c10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{58}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18322/selection/6c339bbbf680fd438fc4befc8d333c50832dd8fcaec7fc0032cffd699a749572" :answer/id #uuid "7cc1a12e-1ec9-5610-8c5d-5006261870cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{70}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18322/selection/f3a7563fe91612b462c80b1302816c8c3d2939b1291369ee5d2ca428e1a26e8a" :answer/id #uuid "b8ad0921-944f-5bea-ad24-07d4f0f5bfa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{113}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18322/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7d239a0-5555-5a5f-8e7c-5541a5a59980" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18322/selection/5925bef74d9593b1a517c264a2c49ec5b06eb1da01b8b814c5455bf64faa0c2d" :answer-field/choices ["q-18322/selection/983df087e2774509d32bf4ada481607a259c849b95031608b49f845cd218a233" "q-18322/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" "q-18322/selection/5925bef74d9593b1a517c264a2c49ec5b06eb1da01b8b814c5455bf64faa0c2d" "q-18322/selection/6c339bbbf680fd438fc4befc8d333c50832dd8fcaec7fc0032cffd699a749572" "q-18322/selection/f3a7563fe91612b462c80b1302816c8c3d2939b1291369ee5d2ca428e1a26e8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18322" :question/id #uuid "c70e65b8-080c-5852-97fc-a933e5e34270" :question/math-academy-id "q-18322" :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(1,0,-2)$, $B(1,2,4)$, and $C(3,-2,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨1,0,-2⟩,\\,b=⟨1,2,4⟩,\\,c=⟨3,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨1,2,4⟩-⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,2,6⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩-⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 3}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{40}\\cdot \\sqrt{17}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{170}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{170}})≈{58}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-18322/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18322"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-19110"] :question/problem "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(0,4,5)$, $Q(1,5,4)$, and $R(2,3,6).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨0,4,5⟩,\\,q=⟨1,5,4⟩,\\,r=⟨2,3,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨1,5,4⟩-⟨0,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨2,3,6⟩-⟨0,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(0)={90}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-77165/selection/9942f8783b1d615a7489a5d03bc2b1bf310955074c87b33dee81f9e73803b153" :answer/id #uuid "84bb65f9-fe22-5996-8f58-e03a81a38199" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{66.42}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77165/selection/405e9642c04dae34409d247313ba0efc305e3c34363ebb382bb3bbe894788b4b" :answer/id #uuid "a600b8de-19f2-5c16-8bbb-3db6c5396720" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{64.52}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77165/selection/6f5e64352976f7265d79d9f929fbd362bd53b01b6aa03c33e4f045230fd9cb6a" :answer/id #uuid "b6d0008a-17c7-5148-a615-14be8fa49411" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{53.13}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77165/selection/0899c3fb9ccd229235ee06edc225ed5f4146ac9adb60b09dac43a9cc4b7326df" :answer/id #uuid "52d09f0d-ef08-51ed-9676-488cfd7fd686" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{84.26}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77165/selection/9a4203f0fa4a912d9aaa0dcf8d1c42b2d6c12773817304dbb7e2c0c5ba296030" :answer/id #uuid "908967fd-9f87-517e-b14e-dd9063dc0012" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{78.46}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77165/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "70c3f7dc-1cfb-5635-be40-ad2dadddc2e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77165/selection/9942f8783b1d615a7489a5d03bc2b1bf310955074c87b33dee81f9e73803b153" :answer-field/choices ["q-77165/selection/9942f8783b1d615a7489a5d03bc2b1bf310955074c87b33dee81f9e73803b153" "q-77165/selection/405e9642c04dae34409d247313ba0efc305e3c34363ebb382bb3bbe894788b4b" "q-77165/selection/6f5e64352976f7265d79d9f929fbd362bd53b01b6aa03c33e4f045230fd9cb6a" "q-77165/selection/0899c3fb9ccd229235ee06edc225ed5f4146ac9adb60b09dac43a9cc4b7326df" "q-77165/selection/9a4203f0fa4a912d9aaa0dcf8d1c42b2d6c12773817304dbb7e2c0c5ba296030"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77165" :question/id #uuid "e38d8e83-96eb-54fa-b9d4-c3057eacb534" :question/math-academy-id "q-77165" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(5,3t+2,2),$ $B(1,3t,2)$ and $C(1,4t,3).$ Find $∠ABC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{BA}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{BC}=4.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨5,\\,3t+2,\\,2⟩,\\,b=⟨1,\\,3t,\\,2⟩,\\,c=⟨1,\\,4t,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠ABC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/assets/2c81d48afacc4ac5e81ab501bc713009ea4425451fcf8dbf414672aeadbb1679.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{BA}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{BC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA} & =a-b \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,3t+2,\\,2⟩-⟨1,\\,3t,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{BC} & =c-b \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4t,\\,3⟩-⟨1,\\,3t,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{BA}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{BC}=4$, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{BC} & =4 \\\\ 4\\cdot 0+2\\cdot t+0\\cdot 1 & =4 \\\\ 0+2t+0 & =4 \\\\ 2t & =4 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA} & =⟨4,2,0⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{BC} & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{BA}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{BC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{BA}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{BC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{BA}||\\overset{\\to }{BC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{20}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{100}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{5})≈{66.42}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-77165/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77165"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-101517/selection/6beb615d335ed1bad436e1e75aa79937c5dbe913ccc036e010f9171f9a4386ce" :answer/id #uuid "e7607c45-5946-5e09-8e46-93b4cbfdf214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{77.21}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101517/selection/7f9275729231b54e211335067263659179abb222dca2654efdc1fbb328f15a23" :answer/id #uuid "a371afc8-0ab5-56aa-9ecd-fcc72a15a54d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{79.84}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101517/selection/9b59cc46136b35e7a2f6f26046ab28a728ddb8896e4ae6267067ef2a4977da39" :answer/id #uuid "053f1e8f-6088-5c59-b0e7-80c34f51dd02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{73.42}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101517/selection/070831a1157cabbf0a129d1826f6b35a65313d39250d455b380805659418423b" :answer/id #uuid "4b413d0d-adcc-5ede-88f1-f525f73eea61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{75.63}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101517/selection/b626a304b2c455729c354c8ea163d50cc6bf452decf0d8f942d9d4f943a4e2bc" :answer/id #uuid "27f2d286-92ed-577b-a2e7-38b423d4a591" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{71.36}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101517/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15ab182e-bbfb-5624-8909-cb1e05f3c135" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101517/selection/070831a1157cabbf0a129d1826f6b35a65313d39250d455b380805659418423b" :answer-field/choices ["q-101517/selection/6beb615d335ed1bad436e1e75aa79937c5dbe913ccc036e010f9171f9a4386ce" "q-101517/selection/7f9275729231b54e211335067263659179abb222dca2654efdc1fbb328f15a23" "q-101517/selection/9b59cc46136b35e7a2f6f26046ab28a728ddb8896e4ae6267067ef2a4977da39" "q-101517/selection/070831a1157cabbf0a129d1826f6b35a65313d39250d455b380805659418423b" "q-101517/selection/b626a304b2c455729c354c8ea163d50cc6bf452decf0d8f942d9d4f943a4e2bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101517" :question/id #uuid "840ed0f5-3459-5b4f-a6cd-56893ad1441d" :question/math-academy-id "q-101517" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(2t,-1,5)$, $B(-3,t,1)$ and $C(2t+1,2,-t).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=5.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2t,\\,-1,\\,5⟩,\\,b=⟨-3,\\,t,\\,1⟩,\\,c=⟨2t+1,\\,2,\\,-t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,t,\\,1⟩-⟨2t,\\,-1,\\,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3-2t,\\,t+1,\\,-4⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨2t+1,\\,2,\\,-t⟩-⟨2t,\\,-1,\\,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,3,\\,-t-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=5$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =5 \\\\ (-3-2t)\\cdot 1+(t+1)\\cdot 3+-4\\cdot (-t-5) & =5 \\\\ -3-2t+3t+3+4t+20 & =5 \\\\ 5t+20 & =5 \\\\ 5t & =-15 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨-3-2(-3),(-3)+1,-4⟩, \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,-4⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =1,\\,3,\\,-(-3)-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{29}\\cdot \\sqrt{14}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{406}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{406}})≈{75.63}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-101517/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101517"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124813/selection/63a57e449df15fa97e620902347dae141a4b773c20487b8ddcdb453244933c6a" :answer/id #uuid "726f5315-901e-